{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1214413-da-mage-additional-material","id":1214413,"title":"DA:Mage-Additional Material?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-02T21:11:50-07:00","id":1214413,"title":"DA:Mage-Additional Material?","content":"Hello! I've recently gotten ahold of both the DA:Mage books for a decent price and I've been working on a generational campaign set in the East. While the Spirit Talker is appropriate for many Animist groups I was hoping to find something more in line with other possible groups in the area like the Wu Lung and other Magi like the Akashics. If possible can anyone point me the right direction? Official or fan made, Im happy to look at just about anything to run with the systems of DA:Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T01:16:39-07:00","id":1214471,"title":"","content":"Dragons of the East could be of interest to you. It\u2019s not a DA book, but it has a good history section with tonnes of spirits for the region and a whole section on the Wu Lung and the akashics, and another on all the other mystics one may encounter, including a whole new (and now horribly out of date) Eastern technocracy counterpart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 05-04-2018, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T01:35:08-07:00","id":1214479,"title":"","content":"There has been a couple of threads here on the forum in the past discussion Foundation and Pillars for Akashics. Might want to search for those. Can't remember there being a discussion about the Wu Lung though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T09:10:05-07:00","id":1215091,"title":"","content":"If you're looking for another pillar-foundation set being used in India, there's information on that in the archaic sorcery section of V20's Black Hand supplement.<br /> It's way different that akashic magic, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T19:18:05-07:00","id":1215320,"title":"","content":"At some point, I think Malcolm Shepherd, who wrote the revised Akashic Brotherhood book as well as the Akashic and Wu Lung material in Dragons of the East, posted an unofficial Foundation and Pillars set for Dark Ages Akashics, but for the life of me I can't find it. <br /> <br /> For the Wu Lung, I always sort of suspected that their Foundation would be the Yellow Mountain of Earth, with their Pillars being the White Tiger of Metal, the Yellow Phoenix of Fire, the Green Dragon of Wood and the Black Tortoise Warrior of Water, or something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T07:14:48-07:00","id":1215476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1214413-da-mage-additional-material?p=1215320#post1215320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At some point, I think Malcolm Shepherd, who wrote the revised Akashic Brotherhood book as well as the Akashic and Wu Lung material in Dragons of the East, posted an unofficial Foundation and Pillars set for Dark Ages Akashics, but for the life of me I can't find it.<br /> <br /> For the Wu Lung, I always sort of suspected that their Foundation would be the Yellow Mountain of Earth, with their Pillars being the White Tiger of Metal, the Yellow Phoenix of Fire, the Green Dragon of Wood and the Black Tortoise Warrior of Water, or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kept a copy:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Foundation: Vajra (&quot;diamond&quot; or &quot;thunderbolt&quot;) representing the dynamic potential of enlightnement. Some tibetan Akashics call thinks Dralaphurba (&quot;windhorse-thunder&quot;) which will later be known as Draladhrama.<br /> <br /> Their aura penalizes rolls that require expressing intimacy.<br /> <br /> Rank 1: normal &amp; supernatural Social rolls have a +1 difficulty due to the Akashic's subtle nature.<br /> <br /> Rank 3: Attempts to alter the Akashic's mind with supernatural powers face a +1 difficulty penalty since the Akashic's mind becomes consumed with esoteric symbols wrapped around and transcendant empty space.<br /> <br /> Rank 5: The Akashic's body now obeys formless, esoteric patterns that are almost unpredictable. Opponents now face a +1 difficulty penalty to strike with physical attacks, unless they target the character's pattern.<br /> <br /> <br /> Pillars: &quot;Kaya&quot; ('bodies'). These correspond to the different paths to enlightenment and the different elemental symbols of reality.<br /> <br /> - Nirmanakaya is the Scarlet Phoenix-Body. This corresponds to the physical body, as well as practices based on everyday observance and society at large. Many physical applications of Do spring from this Pillar. This Pillar is rigid and emphasizes custom.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Sambhokaya is the Pearl Tiger-Body. It is the Pillar of communication and of opening oneself to invisible realms. Akashic who deal with the gods make use of this kaya.<br /> <br /> - Dharmakaya is also called the Dragon-Body and represents the dissolution of preconceived ideas. Akashic tap this with internal martial arts, quiet meditation and austerity. The student leaves behind illusions to see things as they are, leading to simple but powerful magic.<br /> <br /> - Swabhavakaya, the Windhorse-Body is the path of black magic and quick, brutal esoteric training. It transforms the Akashic into a living mystical symbol, able to change other symbols and thus creatures attached to them. It includes dangerous arts like karma manipulation.<br /> <br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> Quote:<br /> Foundation:<br /> <br /> In this period, we call the Foundation the Vajra (&quot;diamond&quot; or &quot;thunderbolt&quot;),<br /> represented the dynamic potential of anlightenment. Some Tibetan Akashics will<br /> call it Dralaphurba (&quot;windhorse-thunder&quot;) which will later be known as<br /> Draladhrama, the modern syncretic term. Their aura penalizes rolls which require<br /> expressing intimacy.<br /> <br /> Akashics have an aura of emptiness, like they are a vast, empty space that<br /> consumes the unprepared.<br /> <br /> Rank 1: Normal and supernatural Social rolls have a +1 difficulty due to the<br /> Akashic's subtle nature.<br /> <br /> Rank 3: Attempts to alter the Akashic's mind with supernatural powers (Doiminate,<br /> Obligation, Crona, etc.) face a +1 difficulty penalty since the Akashic's mind<br /> becomes consumed with esoteric symbols wrapped around an empty space.<br /> <br /> Rank 5: The Akashic's body now obeys formless, esoteric patterns that are almost<br /> unpredictable. Opponents now face a +1 difficulty penalty to strike with physical<br /> attacks, unless they directly target the character's pattern.<br /> <br /> Pillars:<br /> <br /> The four pillars are called &quot;kaya&quot; (&quot;bodies&quot;). These correspond to the different<br /> paths to enlightenment and the different elemental symbols of reality.<br /> <br /> The Nirmanakaya is the Scarlet Phoenix-Body. This corresponds to the the physical<br /> body, as well as practices based on everyday observance and society at large.<br /> Many physical applications of Do sping from this Pillar. This Pillar is rigid and<br /> emphasizes custom.<br /> <br /> Rank 1: Sense the flow of propriety in a being or place; whether a person is<br /> healthy, whether Quintessence flows naturally through a place (instaed of being<br /> twisted or snagged) and whether a person is speaking honestly.<br /> <br /> Rank 2: Can use proper medicine and exercise to heal oneself of bashing or lethal<br /> damage, can smooth chi flow along its proper course (but not determine what that<br /> course is; he can return strength to a Dragon Nest, but not add extra strength to<br /> it) and can detect supernatural compulsion in others and ward it off in himself.<br /> <br /> Rank 3: Learns proper rigid forms to increase physical prowess, medicine to heal<br /> bashing and lethal in others and aggravated in himself. The Akashic can also ward<br /> off supernatural compulsion in a person or area.<br /> <br /> Rank 4: The Akashic can force people or spirits to obey any vow they willingly<br /> make. He can heal aggravated wounds in others by using traditional medicine and<br /> sustain his body with discipline so strong that it can ward off fire and shatter<br /> swords and spears.<br /> <br /> Rank 5: The Akashic is a disciplined master of external rigid power and internal<br /> sensitivity to the structure of the Tapestry. He can enter Heaven (the Astral<br /> Umbra) at will and cannot be cut off from the universe, since he can use rites<br /> and exercises to take chi from anywhere.<br /> <br /> The Sambhokaya is the Pearl Tiger-Body. It is the Pillar of communication and of<br /> opening oneself to invisible realms. Akashic who deal with the gods make use of<br /> this kaya.<br /> <br /> Rank 1: The Akashic can peer into the Umbra and can improve his ability to<br /> communicate (-1 difficulty/success), but not use telepathy or languages that he<br /> does not know. He can see if active spirits are possessing people or places.<br /> <br /> Rank 2: The Akashic can sense emotions and can engage in voluntarily telepathic<br /> speech with others, including spirits on the other side of the Umbra.<br /> <br /> Rank 3: The Akashic can telepathically communicate with anyone and can even<br /> overcome resistance. He can enter dreams and send terrible visions (inflicting<br /> bashing damage) to people or spirits. He can even reach into the Umbra while<br /> staying in the normal world.<br /> <br /> Rank 4: Communication with even slumbering spirits is possible, and the Akashic<br /> can even speak to past incarnations of entities through the Akashic Record. The<br /> mage can makes spirits visible and tangible to others, as well. All this<br /> information allows him to avoid surprise and improve alertness with bonuses to<br /> defensive dice pools.<br /> <br /> Rank 5: Akashics can communicate with something to the extent that they become<br /> that thing, animating a statue, rock, person or spirit, whether they like it or<br /> not. The character can also speak directly to patterns allowing him to animate or<br /> destroy them (aggravated, resisted by Willpower).<br /> <br /> The Dharmakaya is also called the Dragon-Body and represents the dissolution of<br /> preconceived ideas. Akashic tap this with internal martial arts, quiet meditation<br /> and austerity. The student leaves behind illusions to see things as they are,<br /> leading to simple but powerful magic.<br /> <br /> Rank 1: The Akashic can see through illusions, including mundane disguises and<br /> magical deceptions, and even fients and distractions in combat (grants an<br /> initiative bonus)<br /> <br /> Rank 2: You would say that the Akashic could &quot;divide&quot; his mind, but really, the mind expands to encompass many things. A spell allows the character to fully concentrate on multiple nonmagical actions (1 for each arm in addition to one spell, usually). The Akashic can also let his sense of self dissolve, becoming silent or invisible.<br /> <br /> Rank 3: The Akashic abandons egotism in movement and sees that time is arbitrary (allowing multiple actions) and sees the natural flaws in structure (allowing extra damage). He can also honestly judge the abilities of others (determining their traits with a spell, so long as the character could see them in action).<br /> <br /> Rank 4: The character's sense of place is an illusion; he can teleport from place<br /> to place and affect things from a distance.<br /> <br /> rank 5: The mage can now be many places at once and can provide minds for each<br /> node of experience. He realizes all living chi belongs to a single, cosmic flow<br /> and can siphon it to and from other creatures.<br /> <br /> Swabhavakaya, the Windhorse-Body is the path of black magic and quick, brutal<br /> esoteric training. It tranforms the Akashic into a living mystical symbol, able<br /> to change other symbols and thus, the creatures attached to them. It includes<br /> dangerous arts like karma manipulation.<br /> <br /> Rank 1: By studying omens and meditative visions, the character can sense the odds of a future event and recognize mighty or infamous destinies.<br /> <br /> Blah, blah, blah. You guys do the rest. </div> </div> </div>He also did a version for the Chakravanti, but I believe that material got used to create the sorcerers in Black Hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}